question:
The Geriatric ED (GED) Guidelines developed by ACEP, SAEM, 
AGS, and ENA make recommendations in all of the following areas 
except:

englishExplanation:
The GED guidelines consist of 40 specific recommendations in six general categories: (1) staffing and administration; 
(2) equipment and supplies; (3) education; (4) policies, procedures, 
and protocols; (5) follow-up and transitions of care; and (6) qualityimprovement measures.
